ACME CORP - LATE ADDENDUM & COMPLIANCE MANDATE
Document ID: ACME-ADDENDUM-2024-Q3-09
Date: September 29, 2024
Author: Marcus Vance (CISO Office, Acme Commercial Corp)
Classification: Urgent / Executive Mandate

CRITICAL NEW REQUIREMENT FOR TOMORROW'S DEMO:
Due to Acme's expansion into commercial healthcare and life sciences client onboarding, the prospective solution MUST satisfy the following immediate compliance prerequisites:

1. Business Associate Agreement (BAA) Support:
The content platform and AI agent pipeline must be fully HIPAA-compliant with formal BAA execution capabilities.

2. PHI Automated Redaction / Masking:
Any ingested tax packets or identity documentation containing Protected Health Information (PHI) or patient identifiers must be flagged and masked before indexing into general workflow streams.

3. Dedicated US-East Healthcare Vaulting:
All healthcare commercial onboarding assets must be cryptographically pinned to US-East data centers with customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK).

ACTION FOR DEMO TEAM:
Please ensure tomorrow's demonstration includes a dedicated walkthrough of Box Governance classification tags for HIPAA/PHI and demonstrates automated BAA contract generation.
